{
  "source": "internet_archive",
  "identifier": "twainsfeastsearc0000beah_l5f4",
  "title": "Twain's feast : searching for America's lost foods in the footsteps of Samuel Clemens",
  "creator": "Beahrs, Andrew, 1973-",
  "year": 2010,
  "subject": [
    "Twain, Mark, 1835-1910",
    "Gastronomy",
    "Cooking, American",
    "Food habits -- United States"
  ],
  "description": [
    "323 p. ; 24 cm",
    "Shares insights into Mark Twain's menu-style tribute to American cuisine and how it included wild regional specialties that have been lost to industrial food production, tracing the author's efforts to track down eight specific dishes",
    "Includes bibliographical references and index",
    "It makes me cry to think of them : prairie-hens, from Illinois -- A barrel of odds and ends : possum and raccoon -- Masterpiece of the universe : trout at Lake Tahoe -- Heaven on the half shell : oysters and mussels in San Francisco -- Dinner was leisurely served : Philadelphia terrapin -- The most absorbing story in the world : sheep-head and croakers, from New Orleans -- It is my Thanksgiving Day : cranberries -- Twilight : maple syrup -- Epilogue"
  ],
